#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""afc-chat: provider-agnostic unified CLI UI for Agentic CLI Fleet (ACF).

Runs Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI or Antigravity (agy) behind one clean terminal
interface so every inference provider renders the exact same workflow:

  - Short task checklist box (when the agent creates steps / todos / task.md)
  - 1-line live running bash / tool indicator underneath (with elapsed time & tokens)
  - Collapsed 1-line step summary when the turn finishes (Ctrl+O or /steps to expand)
  - Clean final response inline (keeping tmux's scrollback, thin scrollbar and mouse copy)

Usage:
  afc-chat [--tool claude|codex|gemini|agy] [--account NAME] [--mode auto|plan|bypass]
           [--resume ID | --continue] [--model ID] [--effort LEVEL]
           [--checklist auto|on|off] [--prompt TEXT] [--once TEXT] [--wait SECONDS]
  afc-chat claude|codex|gemini|agy [options...]

Slash commands inside the chat:
  /steps [N|full]              expand the bash/tool steps & outputs of the last turn (or turn N)
  /tasks                       show the current task checklist
  /mode [auto|plan|bypass]     show or change permission mode (Shift+Tab cycles)
  /model [set] <id>            show or change model (also works with Alt+M)
  /effort <level>              show or change reasoning effort (claude, codex, agy)
  /provider <tool> [account]   switch inference provider in this pane
  /checklist [auto|on|off]     control checklist prompting (auto = native, on = nudge)
  /new  | /clear               start a fresh conversation
  /native                      hand off to this provider's native interactive CLI on the same chat
  /help                        show commands and shortcuts
  /quit                        exit (or Ctrl+D)
"""
